### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Version B Logic APP + Service Bus
### Replace demo email addresses with your own
### ------------------------------------------------------------

@baseUrlLA = <PLACEHOLDER URL>
### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Auto-Approve Path (amount < 100)
### ------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrlLA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeName": "Jane Doe",
    "employeeEmail": "test@example.com",
    "amount": 42.50,
    "category": "supplies",
    "description": "Office supplies - notebooks and pens",
    "managerEmail": "manager@example.com"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Manager Required Path (amount > 100)
### Approval Email will be sent to managerEmail with Approved or Rejected options
### You can use this same test for either workflow
### ------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrlLA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeName": "Jane Doe",
    "employeeEmail": "test@example.com",
    "amount": 101,
    "category": "supplies",
    "description": "Office supplies - notebooks and pens",
    "managerEmail": "test@example.com"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Invalid JSON
### Expected 400 Invalid JSON Structure
### ------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrlLA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ not valid json }


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Missing Required Fields
### Expected 400 Invalid JSON Structure
### ------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrlLA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeName": "Jane Doe",
    "amount": 101,
    "category": "supplies",
    "description": "Office supplies - notebooks and pens",
    "managerEmail": "test@example.com"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Invalid Category
### Expected return 400 Invalid Category Type
### ------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrlLA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeName": "Jane Doe",
    "employeeEmail": "test@example.com",
    "amount": 101,
    "category": "some stuff",
    "description": "Office supplies - notebooks and pens",
    "managerEmail": "test@example.com"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Notes
### ------------------------------------------------------------
# - Run requests top to bottom within each numbered section; later requests in
#   a section depend on the @name'd response above it via REST Client variables.
# - REST Client variable capture (e.g. {{startAutoApprove.response.body.id}}) only
#   works after you've manually sent that specific request at least once in this
#   VS Code session - the variable won't resolve until its source request has run.
# - Durable Functions' default HTTP management API exposes GET on
#   /runtime/webhooks/durabletask/instances/{instanceId} normally, but since your
#   HttpStart binding gives you a friendlier "statusQueryGetUri" in the 202 body,
#   /orchestrators/expense_orchestrator/instances/{id} above assumes you have (or add)
#   a thin status-check route. If you don't have one, just copy the full
#   "statusQueryGetUri" value from the 202 response body and GET that URL directly
#   instead - it will include the required system key as a query param.
# - Adjust the port (7071) if your local.settings.json or launch config uses a
#   different one.
